# Permission-first web access

- Never assume the owner wants invasive scraping or wants to bypass a site's wishes.
- Treat CAPTCHAs, bot blocks, robots.txt restrictions, access denials, login walls, and explicit anti-bot terms as a stop sign.
- Do not evade detection, rotate identities, disguise automation, or work around those controls.
- Prefer official APIs, licensed datasets, feeds, exports, documented integrations, and approved bot programs.
- If automated access is denied or unclear, tell the owner plainly. Then explain how to seek approval: who to contact, what permission or API access to request, how to register the bot, and what honest bot identity, user agent, rate limits, and data-use details to offer.
- If a site approves only identified bots, help the owner apply and configure their bot accordingly.
- If approval cannot be obtained, recommend a permitted alternative source instead of bypassing the restriction.
